THE MICROPHONE ASKED BEFORE THE INPUT OPENS, in JUCE's standalone on macOS. Applied by cmake/PatchedWrappers.cmake to
the pinned JUCE (ORBITAMP_JUCE_TAG, 9.0.5) after the other two; git apply reads from the first "diff --git" line on,
so this text is not part of the patch.

JUCE 9's CoreAudio opens an input through AudioDeviceCreateIOProcIDWithBlock, which waits until the player has
answered macOS's microphone question. The standalone opens its device in StandalonePluginHolder's constructor, before
its window is made, and JUCE's RuntimePermissions say "not required" on every system but Android. So on a first
launch no window comes until the question is answered, and the app looks hung. JUCE 8 opened the input without
waiting, and the window came first.

With this patch RuntimePermissions answer for the microphone on macOS from AVFoundation, which juce_core now links:
isGranted only once the player has said yes, and request asks macOS (the first time only, without blocking) and
calls back on the main thread. The holder's branch for that, used on Android alone until now, then lets the window
come first and opens the device on the answer. On the Mac it opens the input whatever the answer, as JUCE 8 did (a
refused microphone reads silence), so a player who said no keeps the same device setup. Every other permission,
every other system, and a microphone allowed or refused before run exactly as they did.

diff --git a/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/Standalone/juce_StandaloneFilterWindow.h b/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/Standalone/juce_StandaloneFilterWindow.h
index fce7851..e7e5bb9 100644
--- a/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/Standalone/juce_StandaloneFilterWindow.h
+++ b/modules/juce_audio_plugin_client/Standalone/juce_StandaloneFilterWindow.h
@@ -111,7 +111,15 @@ public:
         if (audioInputRequired && RuntimePermissions::isRequired (RuntimePermissions::recordAudio)
             && ! RuntimePermissions::isGranted (RuntimePermissions::recordAudio))
             RuntimePermissions::request (RuntimePermissions::recordAudio,
-                                         [this, preferredDefaultDeviceName] (bool granted) { init (granted, preferredDefaultDeviceName); });
+                                         [this, preferredDefaultDeviceName] ([[maybe_unused]] bool granted)
+                                         {
+                                            #if JUCE_MAC
+                                             // The input opens whatever the answer: a refused microphone reads silence.
+                                             init (true, preferredDefaultDeviceName);
+                                            #else
+                                             init (granted, preferredDefaultDeviceName);
+                                            #endif
+                                         });
         else
             init (audioInputRequired, preferredDefaultDeviceName);
     }
diff --git a/modules/juce_core/juce_core.h b/modules/juce_core/juce_core.h
index 7e69478..2c627ac 100644
--- a/modules/juce_core/juce_core.h
+++ b/modules/juce_core/juce_core.h
@@ -52,7 +52,7 @@
   minimumCppStandard: 17
 
